// REJECTS: Unexpected token ''1234''
//
// `port: '1234';` on a Trino specification. Trino types its port as INTEGER, so the quoted
// form does not parse -- the opposite of MemSql and Databricks, which type theirs as STRING
// and reject the bare integer (./neg-memsql-port-integer-literal.pure).
//
// The two fixtures are a matched pair on purpose. The same field name, in two connection
// blocks a user would consider interchangeable, has two mutually exclusive spellings, and
// neither vendor's grammar hints at which camp it is in. A rewrite that accepts both forms
// everywhere passes every positive fixture in ../fixtures/ and is wrong about eight grammars.
//
// Trino's INTEGER camp also holds Redshift `port`, Oracle `port`, Aurora `port` and Spanner
// `proxyPort`, all verified against this runner.
###Connection
RelationalDatabaseConnection fixture::neg::TrinoStringPort
{
  store: fixture::neg::Db;
  type: Trino;
  specification: Trino
  {
    host: 'trino.example.com';
    port: '1234';
    catalog: 'tpch';
    schema: 'tiny';
  };
  auth: Test;
}
